# Simple Sweave Example

by Friedrich Leisch, Vincent Goulet and R Core Team

In this simple example we embed parts of the examples from the
`kruskal.test` help page into a HTML document:

<!-- begin.rcode -->
data(airquality, package="datasets")
library("stats")
kruskal.test(Ozone ~ Month, data = airquality)
<!-- end.rcode -->

The usage of the `kruskal.test()` function is

<pre><code class='language-R'>kruskal.test(x, ...)

## S3 method for class 'formula'
kruskal.test(formula, data, subset, na.action, ...)
</code></pre>



The location parameter of the Ozone distribution varies
significantly from month to month. We include a boxplot of the
data with the following code:

<!-- begin.rcode label=boxp, eval=FALSE -->
boxplot(Ozone ~ Month, data = airquality)
<!-- end.rcode -->

The resulting plot is displayed below.

<!-- begin.rcode fig=TRUE, echo=FALSE -->
library("graphics")
<!-- coderef boxp-->
<!-- end.rcode -->

We end this example with some gratuitous LaTeX math.

$$
X_1, X_2, \dotsc, X_n \sim N(\mu, \sigma^2)
$$

